  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "What is the cardinality of $A\\times B$ for $A={0,1,2,3,...,7}$ and $B={a,b,c,d}?$",
  "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $A$ and $B,$ the cardinality of $A\\times B$ is\n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A\\times B| & =|A|\\cdot |B| \\\\  & =8\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
